<$list filter="[<drillui.samesite>!match[]]" variable="ignore">

<div class="drillui-warn">

CoCalc's project-host proxy sets its session cookies with `SameSite=Lax`, which browsers send on a top-level navigation but never on a cross-site frame load. This wiki is not on that host, so the frame below will get ''401 unauthorized'' no matter which browser you use — the cookie is `HttpOnly`, so no script can supply it. A browser tab is a top-level navigation, which //does// carry a Lax cookie — so use the button below. Serving this wiki from the CoCalc host itself removes the problem entirely: the request is then same-site and the ''auto'' route derives the bridge URL with no configuration.

<a href={{{ [<drillui.url>] }}} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="drillui-open">open drillui in a new tab ↗</a>

</div>

</$list>

<$list filter="[<drillui.mixed>!match[]]" variable="ignore">

<div class="drillui-warn">

This wiki is served over https, so the browser will refuse to embed <$text text={{{ [<drillui.url>] }}}/> — an `http://` frame in an https page is mixed content. Use the ''cocalc'' or ''codespace'' route, both of which are https.

</div>

</$list>

